        "original_id": "20cb823e-caa8-51bf-b8b8-e88b1e157554",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Svalbard, Jan Mayen, Norway, Svalbard and Jan Mayen\n- Systems: ISO 3166-1, ISO 3166-1 numeric, UN M.49\n- Topics: mammal species in Svalbard and Jan Mayen\n\nFacts:\n- ISO 3166-1 defines Svalbard and Jan Mayen as a statistical designation for two parts of Norway under separate jurisdictions: Svalbard and Jan Mayen.\n- Svalbard and Jan Mayen has the ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code SJ, the alpha-3 code SJM, and the numeric code 744.\n- ISO 3166-1 numeric codes are similar to the three-digit country codes maintained by the United Nations Statistics Division and originate from the UN M.49 standard.\n- Svalbard and Jan Mayen has 17 mammal species.\n- In Svalbard and Jan Mayen, 0 mammal species are critically endangered, 3 are endangered, 3 are vulnerable, and 0 are near-threatened.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
